@startuml transient-vs-sustained
title US-04: Transient vs Sustained - Single OUT_OF_RANGE Does Not Alert, Sustained Deviation Does

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\ndeviation.candidates" as DevCandKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\ndeviation-state:{id}\n(hash)" as DevState
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

== Transient OUT_OF_RANGE event (no alert) ==

DevCandKafka -> Evaluator : { entity_id: DEF, status: OUT_OF_RANGE,\n  deviation_metres: 45000, timestamp_ms: T1 }

Evaluator -> DevState : HINCRBY deviation-state:DEF count 1\nHSET episode_start_ms T1 last_processed_ms T1
DevState --> Evaluator : count = 1

Evaluator -> DevState : EXPIRE deviation-state:DEF DEVIATION_STATE_TTL_MS

Evaluator -> Evaluator : count < DEVIATION_SUSTAINED_PINGS\nno alert emitted

note over Evaluator
  A single OUT_OF_RANGE event could be
  a GPS glitch or brief correction.
  Not actionable on its own.
  episode_start_ms records when the deviation began.
end note

== IN_RANGE event - state reset ==

DevCandKafka -> Evaluator : { entity_id: DEF, status: IN_RANGE,\n  timestamp_ms: T2 }

Evaluator -> DevState : DEL deviation-state:DEF
note over Evaluator
  State reset. Transient — no alert raised.
  Deviation Detector observed entity return
  to within corridor threshold (segment distance).
end note

== Sustained deviation (N consecutive OUT_OF_RANGE events) ==

loop for N consecutive OUT_OF_RANGE events
  DevCandKafka -> Evaluator : { entity_id: DEF, status: OUT_OF_RANGE,\n  deviation_metres: 45000, timestamp_ms: Tn }
  Evaluator -> DevState : HINCRBY deviation-state:DEF count 1\nHSET last_processed_ms Tn\nEXPIRE DEVIATION_STATE_TTL_MS
end

DevState --> Evaluator : count >= DEVIATION_SUSTAINED_PINGS

Evaluator -> Kafka : publish ROUTE_DEVIATION alert\n{ entity_id, current_position,\n  deviation_metres, nearest_segment_index,\n  sustained_cycles, episode_start_ms }

@enduml
